## 4. Frontend (React + Vite) Architecture

The frontend is organized cleanly, segregating state-management (Context), pages, reusable UI components, and API client layers.

```
frontend/src/
├── api/                     # API client abstraction (Axios wrappers)
│   ├── axiosClient.js       # Base client with interceptors for JWT injection
│   └── *Api.js              # Bounded endpoints (auth, products, orders, etc.)
│
├── components/              # Pure presentation UI components
│   ├── common/              # Global elements (Buttons, Inputs, Modals, Spinners)
│   ├── product/             # Cards, grids, filters
│   └── layout/              # Navbar, Sidebar, Footers
│
├── pages/                   # Main page containers (organized by RBAC role)
│   ├── auth/                # Login, Registration
│   ├── student/             # Catalog, reservations, checkout, dashboard
│   ├── vendor/              # Product/inventory upload, analytics dashboards
│   └── admin/               # Audits, approvals, user lists
│
├── context/                 # Context API for auth and global app state
├── routes/                  # React Router config + route guards (ProtectedRoute)
├── hooks/                   # Custom reusable Hooks (useAuth, useFetch)
└── utils/                   # Helper functions (currency formatters, validators)
```

---

## 5. Infrastructure & Orchestration

The project environment is standardized using Docker Compose for reproducibility:
- **`postgres` Service**: Data persistence layer for user, vendor, product, and order records.
- **`redis` Service**: Acts as both a caching layer and Celery message broker.
- **`backend` Service**: Gunicorn/Django REST Framework container.
- **`frontend` Service**: React + Vite development or Nginx static distribution container.
- **`celery` Service**: Background worker processing slow processes (emails, verification updates).